Bugfix: `restore` no longer corrupts partially changed files with multiple hard links

`restic restore --overwrite if-changed` (and `--overwrite always`) replaced
files with more than one hard link by a fresh file, but skipped writing the
blobs that still matched the old content. The restored file then had the
correct size but contained zeros for the unchanged sections. Restic now
discards the previously computed file state when the target file has to be
replaced, so all blobs get rewritten.

https://github.com/restic/restic/issues/22085
